  if (STACK_MAIN_HORIZONTAL.has(comp) || STACK_MAIN_VERTICAL.has(comp)) {...}
  else if (comp === COMPONENT_ZSTACK) {...}
  else if (isGridComponent(comp)) {...}   // my new branch
}
```
The `if (!PROPAGATING.has(comp)) continue;` at the top skips grids! PROPAGATING = VSTACK, HSTACK, ZSTACK, LAZY_VSTACK, LAZY_HSTACK — no grids. So my grid branch is unreachable.

I need to restructure: either add grids to PROPAGATING (but that would make fill-propagation treat grids as propagating — wrong; grids don't propagate fill up per spec), or change the Phase 1 guard to allow grids.

The cleanest: change the Phase 1 guard to `if (!PROPAGATING.has(comp) && !isGridComponent(comp)) continue;` — grids run through Phase 1 for cell alignment but not fill propagation. Actually the grid branch inside only does cell shell positioning (no fill propagation of the container). So let me change the guard.

